1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,151
Veil keeps incoming payments separate while you share one NEAR name.

2
00:00:04,151 --> 00:00:10,331
This recording uses real testnet transactions and a scripted signer, not browser wallet
approvals.

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:16,885
The receiver connects, then enables Veil with one signed message.

4
00:00:16,885 --> 00:00:21,033
The hosted app derives receiving keys in browser memory.

5
00:00:21,033 --> 00:00:26,991
Enabling makes no payment, and the named account's private key stays in the Node signer.

6
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:30,976
Registration publishes public receiving keys.

7
00:00:30,976 --> 00:00:33,519
Matching keys mean the name is already ready.

8
00:00:33,519 --> 00:00:37,299
A new registration requires a small storage deposit on testnet.

9
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:44,773
In a separate session, the sender enters the receiver's name and zero point zero five
NEAR.

10
00:00:44,773 --> 00:00:48,826
Leaving the name field checks that Veil is enabled.

11
00:00:48,826 --> 00:00:53,859
The confirmed receipt shows delivery to a fresh receiving account.

12
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:01,173
Back in the receiver's session, scanning finds the matching payment.

13
00:01:01,173 --> 00:01:08,685
Its destination matches the sender's receipt, and the inbox shows the received balance
with a Spend action.

14
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:13,957
The receiver confirms a small spend back to their named account.

15
00:01:13,957 --> 00:01:16,215
This creates a public link.

16
00:01:16,215 --> 00:01:20,373
A transaction receipt confirms that the receiving account can spend.

17
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:27,653
A third, unsigned session uses the shared auditor key in a masked field.

18
00:01:27,653 --> 00:01:31,676
It finds the same payment with read-only access.

19
00:01:31,676 --> 00:01:34,475
There is no Spend control.

20
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:42,409
Separate evidence from November eleventh, twenty twenty-six, records a verified DAO
payout and one owned payment.

21
00:01:42,409 --> 00:01:45,821
This evidence panel is not DAO interface footage.

22
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:49,904
Veil is a testnet prototype.

23
00:01:49,904 --> 00:01:56,291
Amounts, timing and senders remain public, and spending can link identities.
